FindMySecureEnvironmentXPCService(8)                   System Manager's Manual

NAME
     FindMySecureEnvironmentXPCService – Find My secure environment XPC
     service

SYNOPSIS
     FindMySecureEnvironmentXPCService

DESCRIPTION
     FindMySecureEnvironmentXPCService is an XPC service that provides
     authenticated access to Apple-internal secure environment endpoints on
     behalf of Find My clients.  It handles AppleConnect OAuth authentication,
     session token management, and authenticated request forwarding so that
     client processes do not require direct access to authentication
     credentials.

     The service is launched on demand by launchd(8) when a client connects to
     its Mach service and idle-exits when no connections remain.

     There are no configuration options to FindMySecureEnvironmentXPCService.
     Users should not run it manually.

   Authentication Flow
     When a client sends a request, the service:

           1.   Obtains an AppleConnect OAuth authorization code via
                AppleConnectClient.framework.

           2.   Exchanges the authorization code for a session token from the
                secure environment token endpoint.

           3.   Caches the session token for subsequent requests.

           4.   Injects the session token and environment headers into the
                client's request and forwards it to the backend.

           5.   Returns the response data and HTTP response directly to the
                client.

     If the backend returns HTTP 401, the service invalidates its cached token
     and AppleConnect ticket, re-authenticates, and retries the request once
     before returning the error.

   XPC Interface
     The service exports two methods via the SecureEnvironmentXPCProtocol
     interface:

     fetchSecureEnvironmentToken
             Authenticates and returns a session token string.  Primarily used
             for diagnostics via sptool(8).

     performAuthenticatedRequest
             Accepts an NSURLRequest, injects authentication headers, forwards
             the request, and replies with the response data and
             NSURLResponse.

ENTITLEMENTS
     Clients must possess the com.apple.findmy.secureenvironment.client
     entitlement and declare a Mach service lookup for
     com.apple.findmy.secureenvironment in their entitlements file.
     Connections without the entitlement are rejected.

MACH SERVICE
     com.apple.findmy.secureenvironment

FILES
     /System/Library/PrivateFrameworks/FindMySecureEnvironment.framework/XPCServices/FindMySecureEnvironmentXPCService.xpc
             Service bundle.

     /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.apple.findmy.secureenvironment.plist
             launchd.plist(5) configuration.

